WEBVTT

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.777
What's the matter, Harry?
You look a little pale.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:16.873
I volunteered for a test flight,
not a suicide mission.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.748
How can we put the new
Delta Flyer through her paces

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.286
without taking a few risks?

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.447
Another risk like that,

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:26.287
and we'll have
to rebuild her all over again.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.420
There's a vessel coming up fast
off our starboard beam.

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:33.090
Shields.

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.498
Range: 50 kilometers.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:36.660
Ten.

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.260
It's pulling alongside.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:42.308
Wow, nice ship.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.171
It's scanning us.

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:45.370
This is Lieutenant Tom Paris.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:47.310
Please identify yourself.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.646
Vectored exhaust ports,
accelerated driver coils.

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.913
Your vessel must be fast.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.682
Gets us where we want to go.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:56.983
Check your scanners.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:58.115
You'll see a comet

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.625
on the other side
of the asteroid field.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:03.787
I wonder which of our ships
could get there first.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.922
Sounds like a challenge.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.933
Are you going to accept?

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:11.697
We are not going to race her.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.636
This is a test flight, right?

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:14.638
Yeah, but...

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.937
What better way to test
the new ship than to see

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.942
how it stands up
to a little competition.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.603
We're ready over here.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.341
Should I count to three?

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:24.977
Guess not.

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:20.458
She's a lot more
maneuverable than we are.

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.898
Not that I'm endorsing

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.732
this misguided exercise,
but maybe we can even the odds.

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.603
The new impulse thrusters.

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:30.040
Ah, now, that's the spirit,
Harry.

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:39.576
We're catching up.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.210
100 meters.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.345
Fifty.

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.583
Bring the backup generators
on line

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.454
and reroute power
to the thrusters.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:02.465
And it's the Delta Flyer
by a nose.

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:05.444
Something's wrong with her ship.

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:08.105
The cabin's filling up
with nyocene gas.

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:09.842
Stand by
for emergency transport.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.625
You all right?

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.284
I think so.

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:23.090
I told you
this wasn't a good idea.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:26.620
Oh, does that mean
you're afraid to try again?

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:28.257
Yeah, Harry?

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.631
You afraid?

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:32.193
No. Of course not.

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:35.537
It's just... your ship
is in no shape for a rematch.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:37.940
My power transformer overloaded.

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:40.171
I bet we could find you
a spare back on Voyager.

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.146
We were about to head back
anyway.

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.307
Right, Tom?

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:46.511
Yeah, whatever you say,
Ensign Eager.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.787
I've been looking forward
to my holodeck time all week.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.385
Why can't you borrow three hours
from someone else?

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.623
Yours are the last piece
to the puzzle.

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:04.159
Tom and I have finally managed
to get a weekend off together.

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:06.330
I've been trading favors
with members of the crew,

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:08.169
so that we could get
the holodeck to ourselves.

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:09.367
A romantic getaway?

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:10.807
Well, that's the idea, yes.

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:14.244
Well, ordinarily I wouldn't
hesitate to oblige.

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:15.645
But I've been looking forward

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:17.410
to indulging myself
in a new hobby.

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.075
Something human doctors
have been enjoying

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.278
for centuries.

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:24.285
I've already booked a tee time.

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:28.760
Well, if your "tee time"

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:30.887
is more important
than our happiness...

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:34.126
our first chance
to be alone in months...

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.862
Fine.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.699
Take my three hours.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:40.739
Thank you.

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:43.367
So what program
are you planning to run?

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:45.377
Something new called Gedi Prime.

00:05:45.445 --> 00:05:46.844
I've heard of that.

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:48.346
The vacation paradise

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:50.814
that makes Risa look
like a tourist trap.

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:51.815
Endless kilometers

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:53.875
of crystalline beaches,
mood reefs,

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.113
bioluminescent waterfalls...

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:58.351
And a championship golf course,
if I'm not mistaken.

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.051
Why don't I just join you?

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:02.185
Somehow, I don't think
that would add to the mood.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:04.422
Don't be so sure.

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:06.522
You haven't seen me
in a bathing suit.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.263
Could you hand me
the veridium injector?

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:18.603
Veridium injector.

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:20.646
Uh... let's see.

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:23.307
The one with the long handle.

00:06:25.118 --> 00:06:26.380
Of course.

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:34.816
Comfortable.

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:37.192
My copilot thinks so, too.

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:38.423
Copilot?

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:41.695
I was on my way to meet him
when I ran into you.

00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:46.262
So, tell me more
about where you're from.

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:51.709
It's a small trinary system
about half a parsec from here.

00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:54.542
Three suns... it must make
for some long days.

00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:59.881
Are you always this inquisitive?

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:03.444
That depends
on who I'm talking to.

00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:07.857
Your new power transformer
is installed and ready to go.

00:07:07.927 --> 00:07:09.326
Thanks.

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:11.454
And your impulse drive
is a real beauty.

00:07:11.531 --> 00:07:13.055
I designed it myself.

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:15.327
But I couldn't help noticing

00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:18.632
your warp system
seems so... rudimentary.

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:22.037
Warp's fine, if you like
going fast in a straight line.

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:24.576
But, to me, that's just physics,
not flying.

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:26.578
I guess it's a matter of taste.

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:29.240
Anyway, for the kind of flying
I'm here for,

00:07:29.315 --> 00:07:30.577
warp is not a factor.

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:33.847
The race course is only
two billion kilometers long.

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:35.820
Race course?

00:07:35.888 --> 00:07:38.083
What kind of race course?

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:40.455
The Antarian
Trans-Stellar Rally...

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:43.723
three segments covering
2.3 billion kilometers.

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:46.765
With obstacles ranging
from dwarf star clusters

00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:47.925
to K-class anomalies.

00:07:48.034 --> 00:07:49.934
Two-man crews,
and most importantly

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:52.163
each ship is limited
to sublight speeds.

00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:53.466
It, it's the ultimate test

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.439
of ship design
and piloting skills.

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:59.205
Not to mention a serious drain
on Voyager's resources.

00:07:59.278 --> 00:08:02.042
You're suggesting
we reassign 15 crewmen

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:04.014
to "modify" the Delta Flyer?

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:06.608
The race has very
specific guidelines.

00:08:06.686 --> 00:08:09.519
All the ships have to use
enriched deuterium fuel.

00:08:09.589 --> 00:08:11.887
The Delta Flyer's not
equipped for that.

00:08:11.991 --> 00:08:14.755
Irina agreed to lend us
a fuel converter.

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:16.590
Captain, this race

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:18.493
is more than just
a sporting event.

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:20.862
Until recently,
this region was a war zone.

00:08:20.933 --> 00:08:21.991
Four different species fought

00:08:22.068 --> 00:08:23.399
for nearly a century
to control it.

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:26.438
Now, for the first time,
they're competing peacefully

00:08:26.506 --> 00:08:29.236
to commemorate the new treaty
that ended the war.

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:32.209
This race embodies everything
the Federation values...

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:33.506
a peaceful coexistence,

00:08:33.579 --> 00:08:35.103
free exchange of ideas.

00:08:35.181 --> 00:08:37.046
I think it's a great idea.

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:39.710
- You do?
- You do?

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:41.582
Absolutely.

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:44.919
This competition is just
the sort of break we need.

00:08:44.991 --> 00:08:47.551
It would give us a chance
to make some friends

00:08:47.627 --> 00:08:51.393
and allow the crew a little R&amp;R.

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:54.597
Request granted.

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:56.259
Thank you, Captain.

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:58.462
One thing, gentlemen.

00:08:58.538 --> 00:09:00.768
Now that we're in this race,

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.205
we're in it to win.

00:09:02.275 --> 00:09:05.301
After all, Starfleet's honor
is at stake.

00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:07.107
Don't worry.

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:10.046
It's in good hands.

00:09:28.534 --> 00:09:30.161
A little tip, Doc.

00:09:30.236 --> 00:09:34.332
This game was not meant
to be played indoors.

00:09:34.407 --> 00:09:36.500
Here to rub salt in the wound?

00:09:36.576 --> 00:09:37.907
I beg your pardon?

00:09:38.044 --> 00:09:41.775
I planned to be putting
the greens at St. Andrews.

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:45.180
Instead... I'm putting
into beakers in Sick Bay,

00:09:45.251 --> 00:09:46.218
thanks to you.

00:09:46.285 --> 00:09:47.217
Me?

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:48.275
Oh, don't be coy.

00:09:48.354 --> 00:09:49.787
I've already approved
your time off.

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:52.483
The Captain's told you
about the race already?

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:54.287
What race?

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.658
I was referring
to your romantic getaway.

00:09:58.497 --> 00:09:59.589
Oh, no.

00:09:59.665 --> 00:10:02.634
Don't tell me you forgot.

00:10:02.702 --> 00:10:03.634
Uh, do me a favor, Doc.

00:10:03.703 --> 00:10:04.795
Keep a lock on my bio-signs.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:05.802
What for?

00:10:05.871 --> 00:10:07.600
Because in about five minutes,

00:10:07.673 --> 00:10:10.665
there may be a medical emergency
in Engineering.

00:10:11.811 --> 00:10:15.338
Hmm. Maybe I can get
that tee time back.

00:10:24.957 --> 00:10:26.049
Hi.

00:10:27.259 --> 00:10:28.954
You're early.

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:36.961
You packed?

00:10:37.069 --> 00:10:39.196
Not yet.

00:10:39.271 --> 00:10:42.434
Um... actually...

00:10:42.508 --> 00:10:44.237
there might be a little problem.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:45.675
Problem?

00:10:47.847 --> 00:10:50.179
I have a chance
to pilot the Flyer in a race...

00:10:50.249 --> 00:10:52.444
uh, a really unique race...

00:10:52.518 --> 00:10:55.487
and the Captain thinks
it's a great idea...

00:10:55.554 --> 00:10:59.718
So, I guess I got so excited
that I forgot about our plans.

00:11:00.926 --> 00:11:02.484
But I-I don't have to do it.

00:11:02.561 --> 00:11:04.495
The Captain would understand.

00:11:04.563 --> 00:11:05.689
It's all right.

00:11:05.765 --> 00:11:07.426
No, no,
I should have remembered.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:10.094
It's just that this seemed like
such an amazing opportunity.

00:11:10.169 --> 00:11:11.158
Pilots from all over...

00:11:11.237 --> 00:11:12.966
I said it's okay.

00:11:14.907 --> 00:11:16.238
Really?

00:11:16.308 --> 00:11:19.209
The holodeck
will always be here.

00:11:19.278 --> 00:11:20.745
This race won't.

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:27.175
I do not deserve you.

00:11:27.253 --> 00:11:29.517
You're right about that.

00:11:31.223 --> 00:11:34.818
So, um, we'll plan this vacation
for another time.

00:11:34.894 --> 00:11:36.122
Sure.

00:11:36.195 --> 00:11:38.095
I-I'm going
to make this up to you.

00:11:38.164 --> 00:11:39.654
I promise.

00:11:50.209 --> 00:11:51.767
Late night?

00:11:55.781 --> 00:11:57.180
Can I get you anything?

00:11:57.249 --> 00:11:58.739
No, thanks.

00:12:02.588 --> 00:12:03.850
Are you okay?

00:12:03.923 --> 00:12:05.686
Oh, my feet. Ah.

00:12:05.758 --> 00:12:07.658
I haven't had a chance
to sit down all day.

00:12:07.727 --> 00:12:09.786
If you're thinking
of cheering me up,

00:12:09.862 --> 00:12:11.386
don't bother.

00:12:11.464 --> 00:12:14.024
Hmm. Who, me? Never.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:15.032
And by the way,

00:12:15.101 --> 00:12:16.898
you can have
your holodeck time back.

00:12:16.969 --> 00:12:19.460
What about your weekend
with Tom?

00:12:19.538 --> 00:12:21.972
He just canceled it.

00:12:23.542 --> 00:12:26.807
Does he have any idea
how much planning it took?

00:12:26.879 --> 00:12:28.506
No.

00:12:28.581 --> 00:12:31.072
And you're not going
to tell him, either.

00:12:32.852 --> 00:12:35.685
He just entered this big race,

00:12:35.755 --> 00:12:38.349
and he's really excited, and...

00:12:38.424 --> 00:12:40.790
I don't want
to spoil it for him.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.953
Well, I'm sure if you tell him

00:12:43.028 --> 00:12:45.758
how important
this weekend was to you,

00:12:45.831 --> 00:12:47.059
he'll reconsider.

00:12:47.133 --> 00:12:49.124
Probably.

00:12:49.201 --> 00:12:53.228
But he should be able
to do what makes him happy.

00:12:54.707 --> 00:12:56.572
What about what makes you happy?

00:12:56.642 --> 00:12:59.839
It's time I faced facts,
Neelix.

00:13:02.448 --> 00:13:05.008
Tom and I just don't
belong together.

00:13:06.652 --> 00:13:08.916
Then you're not in love
with him anymore?

00:13:09.054 --> 00:13:11.181
I didn't say that.

00:13:12.558 --> 00:13:16.494
But, B'Elanna, if you still
love each other...

00:13:16.562 --> 00:13:18.553
Maybe that isn't enough.

00:13:18.631 --> 00:13:21.031
Call me a hopeless romantic,

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:23.068
but I still think it is.

00:13:25.538 --> 00:13:27.563
Yeah, well,
there's a Klingon phrase

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:31.201
that my grandmother
used to use... mok'tah.

00:13:31.277 --> 00:13:33.939
It means "bad match."

00:13:35.681 --> 00:13:38.844
That's what Tom and I are.

00:13:38.918 --> 00:13:41.409
I just hate
that it's taken me three years

00:13:41.487 --> 00:13:43.387
to realize it.

00:13:45.391 --> 00:13:48.053
If you're really such a mok'tah,

00:13:48.127 --> 00:13:50.186
it must have been
an awful three years.

00:13:50.262 --> 00:13:52.662
No.

00:13:52.731 --> 00:13:55.199
Tom is a great guy.

00:13:55.267 --> 00:13:58.168
We've had a lot of fun together.

00:13:58.237 --> 00:14:00.637
And that seems to be
enough for him.

00:14:02.107 --> 00:14:05.042
But not for me.

00:14:06.312 --> 00:14:08.837
Why aren't you saying
all this to Tom?

00:14:08.914 --> 00:14:10.506
I plan to.

00:14:10.583 --> 00:14:12.278
After the race.

00:14:12.351 --> 00:14:17.345
By which time, he'll already
have disappointed you again.

00:14:19.325 --> 00:14:22.624
I may not know as much
about Klingon tradition

00:14:22.695 --> 00:14:24.060
as your grandmother,

00:14:24.129 --> 00:14:26.689
but somehow,
keeping Tom in the dark

00:14:26.765 --> 00:14:28.858
doesn't seem very honorable.

00:14:33.606 --> 00:14:35.471
My feet are feeling better.

00:14:35.541 --> 00:14:37.304
I should go back to work.

00:14:43.782 --> 00:14:48.242
Captain's Log,
Stardate 54058.6.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:51.084
Our request to enter
the Delta Flyer into the rally

00:14:51.156 --> 00:14:52.453
has been accepted.

00:14:52.524 --> 00:14:55.960
I'm meeting with the race
coordinator, Ambassador O'Zaal,

00:14:56.061 --> 00:14:57.551
to work out the details.

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:58.892
We have teams
that have traveled

00:14:58.964 --> 00:14:59.896
quite a distance, Captain,

00:14:59.965 --> 00:15:01.592
but none from as far
as the Alpha Quadrant.

00:15:01.667 --> 00:15:03.567
We're always willing to go
that extra light-year

00:15:03.636 --> 00:15:05.069
for a good cause.

00:15:05.137 --> 00:15:08.470
Well, your, uh,
entrance petition

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:09.802
seems to be in order.

00:15:09.875 --> 00:15:11.900
The Delta Flyer
meets our guidelines.

00:15:12.044 --> 00:15:14.103
Now all you have to do is win.

00:15:14.179 --> 00:15:15.305
Something tells me

00:15:15.381 --> 00:15:17.349
the other teams aren't going
to make that too easy.

00:15:17.416 --> 00:15:18.713
Bridge to the Captain.

00:15:18.784 --> 00:15:20.115
Go ahead, Commander.

00:15:20.185 --> 00:15:21.914
There is
an incoming transmission

00:15:21.987 --> 00:15:23.011
for the Ambassador.

00:15:23.088 --> 00:15:24.350
Route it here.

00:15:35.935 --> 00:15:38.096
I asked not to be disturbed.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:40.900
I'm sorry, but the Aksani
are threatening to withdraw

00:15:40.973 --> 00:15:43.806
unless they're allowed to host
the post-race ceremony.

00:15:43.876 --> 00:15:44.900
Did you explain that

00:15:44.977 --> 00:15:46.672
we've already promised
that to the Chessu?

00:15:46.745 --> 00:15:49.612
Yes. They said
that was... unacceptable.

00:15:51.717 --> 00:15:53.412
Arrange for another meeting.

00:15:53.485 --> 00:15:56.283
I'll have to find
some way of appeasing them.

00:15:58.157 --> 00:16:00.489
Well, I hope the race
you just entered

00:16:00.559 --> 00:16:02.322
doesn't end before it begins.

00:16:02.394 --> 00:16:03.520
It's that serious?

00:16:03.595 --> 00:16:05.392
The peace is still very fragile.

00:16:05.464 --> 00:16:07.989
Every decision I make,
no matter how trivial,

00:16:08.067 --> 00:16:09.625
is looked upon as symbolic.

00:16:09.702 --> 00:16:11.693
So, every time
you make a concession

00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:12.896
to one participant...

00:16:13.005 --> 00:16:14.370
Another is offended, yes.

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:15.464
Maybe we can help.

00:16:15.541 --> 00:16:17.532
That would be wonderful,
but how?

00:16:17.609 --> 00:16:19.577
By providing neutral ground

00:16:19.645 --> 00:16:22.409
for the pre and post-race
activities.

00:16:22.481 --> 00:16:24.915
Since we've never taken
sides in your conflict,

00:16:25.017 --> 00:16:27.508
you couldn't be accused
of showing favoritism.

00:16:27.586 --> 00:16:29.315
If your racing skills
are as sharp

00:16:29.388 --> 00:16:30.912
as your diplomatic instincts,

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:32.855
the other teams
won't have a chance.

00:16:46.872 --> 00:16:49.170
There's someone
to watch out for.

00:16:49.241 --> 00:16:50.435
What's his story?

00:16:50.509 --> 00:16:51.806
His name is Assan.

00:16:51.877 --> 00:16:54.641
He was a fighter pilot...

00:16:54.713 --> 00:16:56.476
one of the most ruthless.

00:16:59.651 --> 00:17:01.209
Uh, where you going?

00:17:01.286 --> 00:17:03.846
A little personal
reconnaissance.

00:17:03.922 --> 00:17:05.287
We are the hosts.

00:17:09.194 --> 00:17:10.525
Lieutenant Tom Paris.

00:17:10.596 --> 00:17:12.564
Welcome aboard.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:16.895
Could I get you something?

00:17:17.036 --> 00:17:18.833
A drink?
Something to eat?

00:17:18.904 --> 00:17:20.269
Tour of the ship?

00:17:20.339 --> 00:17:22.637
Were you assigned to serve me?

00:17:22.708 --> 00:17:25.142
Um, not exactly.

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:27.576
Are we friends?

00:17:27.646 --> 00:17:29.170
I guess not.

00:17:29.248 --> 00:17:31.341
Then you must be one
of those pilots

00:17:31.417 --> 00:17:33.783
who believes in the
fellowship of combat.

00:17:35.721 --> 00:17:37.120
Correct me if I'm wrong,

00:17:37.189 --> 00:17:40.522
but I thought this was
a friendly race, not a battle.

00:17:40.592 --> 00:17:42.753
If that's what you believe,

00:17:42.828 --> 00:17:44.955
then you've already lost.

00:17:46.165 --> 00:17:50.431
Well... nice chatting with you.

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:56.130
Learn anything?

00:17:56.208 --> 00:17:58.802
Yeah, I should leave
the hosting to Neelix.

00:17:58.877 --> 00:17:59.935
Joxom.

00:18:00.079 --> 00:18:01.046
Who?

00:18:01.113 --> 00:18:02.671
My copilot.

00:18:02.748 --> 00:18:05.114
Irina. Hi.

00:18:05.184 --> 00:18:06.879
Well. Looks like
they're good friends.

00:18:06.952 --> 00:18:07.976
They're teammates.

00:18:08.053 --> 00:18:08.985
Mm.

00:18:09.054 --> 00:18:11.045
Close...

00:18:11.123 --> 00:18:13.318
personal teammates.

00:18:13.392 --> 00:18:16.020
Oh, it was nice while it lasted.

00:18:16.095 --> 00:18:17.687
Come on.

00:18:20.966 --> 00:18:23.025
Seven, I need you
to run a diagnostic

00:18:23.102 --> 00:18:24.660
on the lateral sensor array.

00:18:24.736 --> 00:18:27.034
As soon as I'm finished.

00:18:27.106 --> 00:18:28.835
With what?

00:18:28.907 --> 00:18:30.374
Plotting the most
efficient course

00:18:30.442 --> 00:18:32.376
for the first segment
of the rally.

00:18:32.444 --> 00:18:35.777
Seems like the entire crew
has come down with race fever.

00:18:35.848 --> 00:18:38.282
Perhaps you could
persuade the Doctor

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:39.817
to develop a vaccine.

00:18:41.453 --> 00:18:44.286
I'm surprised you're
putting time into this.

00:18:44.356 --> 00:18:47.723
Initially, I did find
the activity irrelevant,

00:18:47.793 --> 00:18:49.556
but then I realized
that it's important

00:18:49.628 --> 00:18:50.788
for the crew's morale

00:18:50.863 --> 00:18:52.922
and for my relationship
with Lieutenant Paris.

00:18:52.998 --> 00:18:56.866
Your relationship
with Lieutenant Paris?

00:18:56.935 --> 00:18:59.495
I was speaking professionally.

00:18:59.571 --> 00:19:02.665
I often work with him
on navigational problems.

00:19:02.741 --> 00:19:05.369
He can be an erratic individual.

00:19:05.444 --> 00:19:07.571
But he's also
a very competent officer

00:19:07.646 --> 00:19:09.273
and clearly a skilled pilot.

00:19:09.348 --> 00:19:12.784
It's the erratic individual
that takes getting used to.

00:19:12.851 --> 00:19:14.876
No doubt.

00:19:14.953 --> 00:19:18.218
But I've learned that if
I embrace some of his interests,

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:19.882
support him
in his personal goals,

00:19:19.992 --> 00:19:22.722
we're able to function
more efficiently as crewmates.

00:19:35.707 --> 00:19:37.265
Harry, where have you been?

00:19:37.342 --> 00:19:38.673
Say Qapla'.

00:19:40.779 --> 00:19:43.009
It means success.

00:19:43.081 --> 00:19:44.878
I just wanted
to capture the moment,

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:47.384
not to mention that cute
bewildered expression.

00:19:47.452 --> 00:19:50.148
What are you doing
in that flight suit?

00:19:50.222 --> 00:19:51.519
There's been a change of plans.

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:52.955
I'm your new copilot.

00:19:54.092 --> 00:19:56.458
Look, I don't have time
for practical jokes.

00:19:56.528 --> 00:19:57.756
Neither do I.

00:19:57.829 --> 00:19:59.820
Ready to bring
that impulse drive on line?

00:19:59.898 --> 00:20:00.922
B'Elanna...

00:20:00.999 --> 00:20:03.832
Okay, I was upset
that you canceled our weekend,

00:20:03.902 --> 00:20:05.028
but then I realized...

00:20:05.103 --> 00:20:07.162
why should we spend
this time apart

00:20:07.239 --> 00:20:10.902
when we can be together
doing something you like?

00:20:10.976 --> 00:20:13.410
What about Harry?

00:20:13.478 --> 00:20:17.539
I assigned him to a level-5
diagnostic in Engineering.

00:20:17.616 --> 00:20:18.947
Oh, that's terrible.

00:20:19.051 --> 00:20:20.484
I'm just kidding.

00:20:20.552 --> 00:20:23.419
I told him how hard it was
for us to get time together,

00:20:23.488 --> 00:20:24.477
and he understood.

00:20:24.556 --> 00:20:26.183
Anyway, the way I see it,

00:20:26.258 --> 00:20:29.489
you're trading an Ensign
for a Chief Engineer.

00:20:31.029 --> 00:20:33.361
Well, you don't have
to convince me.

00:20:33.432 --> 00:20:36.833
I couldn't ask
for a better copilot.

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:40.664
Now just remember,
we're not on vacation.

00:20:40.739 --> 00:20:41.967
The point is to win.

00:20:42.074 --> 00:20:44.804
And you know how much
I hate to lose.

00:20:46.912 --> 00:20:48.436
Thrusters on line.

00:20:48.513 --> 00:20:50.845
Opening Shuttle Bay doors.

00:20:53.986 --> 00:20:56.250
The racers are moving
into position.

00:20:59.124 --> 00:21:00.614
Ambassador.

00:21:02.194 --> 00:21:04.094
Welcome to the first running

00:21:04.162 --> 00:21:06.562
of the Antarian
Trans-Stellar Rally.

00:21:06.632 --> 00:21:08.862
This moment
marks a hopeful point

00:21:08.934 --> 00:21:11.494
in our shared history...
a chance to put aside

00:21:11.570 --> 00:21:13.868
old animosities,
and come together

00:21:13.939 --> 00:21:16.669
in a spirit of peace
and friendly competition.

00:21:16.742 --> 00:21:18.369
Good luck to all of you.

00:21:18.443 --> 00:21:20.707
Prepare for the starting signal.

00:21:26.418 --> 00:21:28.716
Captain, the honor is yours.

00:21:29.821 --> 00:21:31.118
Mr. Tuvok.

00:21:32.357 --> 00:21:34.222
Fire.

00:21:59.584 --> 00:22:02.246
We passed two more ships,
three still ahead of us.

00:22:02.321 --> 00:22:03.618
How's my impulse engine?

00:22:03.689 --> 00:22:06.715
Hot, but stable, thanks
to the new fuel converter.

00:22:08.093 --> 00:22:10.254
That was the Number 8 ship.

00:22:10.329 --> 00:22:11.853
Assan.

00:22:11.930 --> 00:22:13.921
Whoever it is just grazed
our shields.

00:22:13.999 --> 00:22:15.466
Port thrusters are off-line.

00:22:15.534 --> 00:22:16.523
Compensating.

00:22:16.601 --> 00:22:18.933
Well, that was an old trick.

00:22:19.071 --> 00:22:22.529
Back at the Academy
we used to call that "scraping."

00:22:22.607 --> 00:22:25.542
Well, Assan just almost
scraped us out of the race.

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:26.872
How are we doing on time?

00:22:26.945 --> 00:22:28.708
20 seconds to the third marker.

00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:31.943
Assan's already rounding it,
thanks to his little tactic.

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:34.951
Well, it's a long race.

00:22:35.087 --> 00:22:37.248
We'll catch him.

00:22:39.024 --> 00:22:40.252
How's our team doing?

00:22:40.325 --> 00:22:42.623
I announced the
Delta Flyer's progress

00:22:42.694 --> 00:22:45.686
over the com 11 minutes ago.

00:22:45.764 --> 00:22:51.202
In a race like this,
11 minutes can be an eternity!

00:22:51.269 --> 00:22:53.703
The Delta Flyer is
in fourth position,

00:22:53.772 --> 00:22:56.070
having completed
62 percent of the course.

00:22:56.141 --> 00:22:57.802
The Aksani vessel is
in third position

00:22:57.876 --> 00:23:00.174
having completed
68 percent of the course.

00:23:00.245 --> 00:23:02.509
You don't make it sound
very exciting.

00:23:02.581 --> 00:23:04.879
I'm relaying
the relevant information.

00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:06.042
It's all in the delivery.

00:23:06.118 --> 00:23:07.085
Do you mind?

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:10.651
Attention, all hands.

00:23:10.722 --> 00:23:12.781
Stand by for a race update!

00:23:12.858 --> 00:23:15.850
With only 58 million kilometers
left in the first segment,

00:23:15.927 --> 00:23:17.861
the Aksani, lmhotep
and Terrellian ships

00:23:17.929 --> 00:23:19.260
are still battling for the lead.

00:23:19.331 --> 00:23:22.198
Wait. The Number 8 ship
just cut off the Number 3

00:23:22.267 --> 00:23:23.291
in the Darla system.

00:23:23.368 --> 00:23:24.858
Now 3's changing course.

00:23:24.936 --> 00:23:26.233
Using the gravity
from a gas giant

00:23:26.304 --> 00:23:28.272
to boost its speed, it's
making up for lost ground!

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:29.705
Sounds like quite a race.

00:23:29.775 --> 00:23:33.472
Apparently, it's all
in the delivery.

00:23:36.415 --> 00:23:38.315
So much for the Aksani.

00:23:38.383 --> 00:23:41.477
Now it's just down
to Irina and Assan.

00:23:41.553 --> 00:23:42.542
In a few minutes,

00:23:42.621 --> 00:23:44.612
they'll just be echoes
in our aft scanners.

00:23:45.724 --> 00:23:47.749
Well, we still got
the Mobius Inversion coming up.

00:23:47.826 --> 00:23:48.918
The what?

00:23:48.994 --> 00:23:51.462
Tell me you read
the course manual.

00:23:51.530 --> 00:23:55.830
I skimmed it... more or less.

00:23:55.901 --> 00:23:58.335
Oh, great.

00:23:58.403 --> 00:24:01.236
So, what exactly is
this Mobius whatever?

00:24:01.306 --> 00:24:02.671
Take a look.

00:24:02.741 --> 00:24:07.007
Covers the entire last third
of the course.

00:24:07.078 --> 00:24:10.673
Level-6 subspace distortions,
gravimetric shears.

00:24:10.749 --> 00:24:13.309
Just think of it
as a little wormhole

00:24:13.385 --> 00:24:14.852
with a big attitude.

00:24:16.855 --> 00:24:19.915
The Terrellian and lmhotep ships
are still in the lead;

00:24:20.058 --> 00:24:21.923
the Delta Flyer trailing
by a few seconds.

00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:24.722
Meanwhile, the two Chessu ships
are continuing to advance

00:24:24.796 --> 00:24:26.423
claiming fourth
and fifth position.

00:24:26.498 --> 00:24:27.624
My weekly security report.

00:24:27.699 --> 00:24:28.631
I'll read it later.

00:24:28.700 --> 00:24:30.668
There are a few matters
we should discuss.

00:24:30.735 --> 00:24:31.861
She said later, Tuvok.

00:24:31.937 --> 00:24:32.904
Something's wrong.

00:24:32.971 --> 00:24:35.303
They're disappearing.

00:24:35.373 --> 00:24:36.931
Radiation
from the Mobius Inversion

00:24:37.008 --> 00:24:38.134
is blocking our sensors.

00:24:38.210 --> 00:24:39.643
How will we track
their progress?

00:24:39.711 --> 00:24:41.508
We can't.
Not until they emerge

00:24:41.580 --> 00:24:43.639
from the other side
of the anomaly.

00:24:43.715 --> 00:24:45.808
Want to talk about
that report now, Tuvok?

00:24:45.884 --> 00:24:48.648
Later, if that's permissible.

00:24:48.720 --> 00:24:50.347
50 meters.

00:24:50.422 --> 00:24:52.083
Forty.

00:24:52.157 --> 00:24:54.250
We can get through.

00:24:54.326 --> 00:24:55.793
No, they're too close
to each other.

00:24:55.861 --> 00:24:57.385
I'm reversing
our deflector polarity.

00:24:57.462 --> 00:24:58.690
It'll repel their shields.

00:24:58.763 --> 00:25:00.958
Why wait for an opening
when you can make one?

00:25:01.066 --> 00:25:01.998
No, it's too risky.

00:25:02.067 --> 00:25:03.056
Too risky?

00:25:03.134 --> 00:25:05.568
That doesn't sound
like the Tom Paris I know.

00:25:05.637 --> 00:25:06.501
What are you doing?

00:25:06.571 --> 00:25:07.765
Deploying auxiliary thrusters.

00:25:07.839 --> 00:25:10.069
We'll need the extra maneuvering
power to get through the gap.

00:25:10.141 --> 00:25:11.073
B'Elanna...

00:25:11.142 --> 00:25:12.439
Just steer the ship.

00:25:22.521 --> 00:25:25.319
It's them. It's the Delta Flyer.

00:25:25.390 --> 00:25:26.914
They're in the lead!

00:25:27.058 --> 00:25:28.787
They're pulling away!

00:25:28.860 --> 00:25:30.191
We did it!

00:25:30.262 --> 00:25:31.422
You should have waited.

00:25:31.496 --> 00:25:32.861
I saw a chance and I too...

00:25:32.931 --> 00:25:33.863
I'm the pilot.

00:25:33.932 --> 00:25:35.866
That means I do the flying.

00:25:35.934 --> 00:25:38.596
Attention all racers.
There's been an accident.

00:25:38.670 --> 00:25:41.662
Stay in order
and shut down your engines.

00:25:57.522 --> 00:25:58.454
Report.

00:25:58.523 --> 00:25:59.956
His condition's stabilizing.

00:26:00.025 --> 00:26:00.957
I should be able to start

00:26:01.026 --> 00:26:02.550
dermal regeneration
in a few hours.

00:26:02.627 --> 00:26:04.527
This was Assan's fault.

00:26:04.596 --> 00:26:05.528
Why?

00:26:05.597 --> 00:26:07.292
He collided with me
so many times

00:26:07.365 --> 00:26:09.060
my shield generator overloaded.

00:26:09.134 --> 00:26:10.567
Joxom's console exploded.

00:26:10.635 --> 00:26:12.068
He's lucky he's alive.

00:26:14.706 --> 00:26:17.197
If I'm guilty of anything,
it's of coming in second,

00:26:17.275 --> 00:26:19.903
a situation I'll remedy
in the next leg.

00:26:20.011 --> 00:26:22.912
You're doing a poor job
of defending yourself.

00:26:22.981 --> 00:26:25.142
We may have had
something to do with this, too.

00:26:25.216 --> 00:26:28.276
We grazed both of their shields
while in the anomaly.

00:26:28.353 --> 00:26:30.617
Intentionally?

00:26:30.689 --> 00:26:32.020
It was a tight course.

00:26:32.090 --> 00:26:34.524
Everyone was flying
very aggressively.

00:26:34.593 --> 00:26:37.027
Your team is not responsible,
Captain.

00:26:37.095 --> 00:26:38.926
My generators were
already overloading

00:26:38.997 --> 00:26:40.123
when they made contact.

00:26:40.198 --> 00:26:42.928
Perhaps none of you
is to blame.

00:26:43.034 --> 00:26:45.730
I found this interfaced

00:26:45.804 --> 00:26:48.102
with her ship's
shield generator.

00:26:48.173 --> 00:26:51.199
I ran an analysis.

00:26:51.276 --> 00:26:52.903
It's a phase inverter,

00:26:52.978 --> 00:26:55.538
designed to cause
a system overload.

00:26:55.614 --> 00:26:56.876
Well, it's hard to believe

00:26:56.948 --> 00:26:59.610
someone would go this far
just to knock a competitor

00:26:59.684 --> 00:27:01.049
out of the race.

00:27:01.119 --> 00:27:02.177
This may be more

00:27:02.253 --> 00:27:05.017
than a simple case
of cheating, Captain.

00:27:05.090 --> 00:27:09.186
I think someone's trying
to end the peace.

00:27:15.367 --> 00:27:16.800
Maybe I'm missing something,

00:27:16.868 --> 00:27:19.393
but we're talking
about a single act of sabotage.

00:27:19.471 --> 00:27:21.302
How does that threaten
your treaty?

00:27:21.373 --> 00:27:23.000
By itself, it wouldn't.

00:27:23.074 --> 00:27:25.474
But we've received
several threats

00:27:25.543 --> 00:27:27.340
of a more serious nature.

00:27:27.412 --> 00:27:28.379
From whom?

00:27:28.446 --> 00:27:30.175
Groups opposed to the alliance...

00:27:30.248 --> 00:27:34.207
arms dealers, isolationists,
political extremists.

00:27:34.285 --> 00:27:36.685
Up until now I wasn't sure
how seriously to take them.

00:27:36.755 --> 00:27:38.382
Clearly, they pose
a security threat.

00:27:38.456 --> 00:27:39.445
Yes, yes.

00:27:39.524 --> 00:27:40.889
We've done everything
we could

00:27:40.959 --> 00:27:41.926
to protect the racers,

00:27:42.060 --> 00:27:43.357
but that may not be enough.

00:27:45.497 --> 00:27:48.398
I don't want to risk
any more lives.

00:27:48.466 --> 00:27:50.559
We should cancel the race

00:27:50.635 --> 00:27:51.602
or at least postpone it,

00:27:51.670 --> 00:27:53.365
until we can guarantee
everyone's safety.

00:27:53.438 --> 00:27:55.929
No. If we stop now,

00:27:56.041 --> 00:27:58.032
we'll be letting
these extremists win.

00:27:58.109 --> 00:28:00.543
She's right.

00:28:03.682 --> 00:28:04.842
Very well, then.

00:28:04.916 --> 00:28:06.611
If that's the consensus,

00:28:06.685 --> 00:28:09.245
we'll resume tomorrow
as scheduled.

00:28:09.320 --> 00:28:10.446
Of course, Captain,

00:28:10.522 --> 00:28:13.150
if you decide to withdraw,
we'd understand.

00:28:13.224 --> 00:28:16.716
Well, the last time I checked,
I believe we were winning.

00:28:23.635 --> 00:28:24.624
There you are.

00:28:24.703 --> 00:28:27.228
Congratulations
on taking the lead.

00:28:27.305 --> 00:28:28.237
Thanks.

00:28:28.306 --> 00:28:30.137
Of course, uh, you're
not going to win.

00:28:30.208 --> 00:28:31.140
Why is that?

00:28:31.209 --> 00:28:32.301
Because we are.

00:28:32.377 --> 00:28:34.436
You're looking
at your new copilot.

00:28:34.512 --> 00:28:36.912
I checked with one
of the race officials.

00:28:37.015 --> 00:28:38.209
It's perfectly legal

00:28:38.283 --> 00:28:42.447
and it's a chance for both of us
to get back in the race.

00:28:42.520 --> 00:28:45.250
I appreciate the gesture,
but my ship's damaged.

00:28:45.323 --> 00:28:46.756
You don't know our Harry.

00:28:46.825 --> 00:28:48.759
Once we sets his mind
on something...

00:28:48.827 --> 00:28:50.351
He'll not only fix
your ship,

00:28:50.428 --> 00:28:51.918
he'll polish the bulkheads.

00:28:51.996 --> 00:28:53.224
How can you turn me down?

00:28:53.298 --> 00:28:56.199
Apparently, I can't.

00:29:02.173 --> 00:29:04.971
Come on, you can say it.

00:29:05.043 --> 00:29:06.738
It's embarrassing.

00:29:06.811 --> 00:29:08.608
I just want to make sure we're
clear on what we're doing.

00:29:10.949 --> 00:29:14.749
"Right at the light,
then readjust my sight."

00:29:14.819 --> 00:29:16.753
Meaning?

00:29:16.821 --> 00:29:19.153
Come about 86 degrees
at the red giant

00:29:19.224 --> 00:29:20.691
then recalibrate sensors

00:29:20.759 --> 00:29:23.250
to compensate
for photonic interference.

00:29:23.328 --> 00:29:24.795
Great. Next?

00:29:24.863 --> 00:29:26.524
Do I really have to spend
my morning

00:29:26.598 --> 00:29:27.758
reciting nursery rhymes?

00:29:27.832 --> 00:29:29.891
It got me through the Academy.

00:29:29.968 --> 00:29:31.595
You were expelled.

00:29:35.073 --> 00:29:37.064
Okay, repeat after me.

00:29:37.142 --> 00:29:38.268
"I am not the pilot.

00:29:38.343 --> 00:29:40.504
I will not attempt
to fly this ship."

00:29:40.578 --> 00:29:43.103
That one doesn't even rhyme.

00:29:45.183 --> 00:29:46.115
Anyone home?

00:29:46.184 --> 00:29:48.414
Well, if it isn't
our competition.

00:29:48.486 --> 00:29:49.612
Here to spy on us?

00:29:49.687 --> 00:29:52.622
I just stopped by to borrow
a hyperspanner.

00:29:52.690 --> 00:29:54.521
Looks like you didn't
get much sleep.

00:29:54.592 --> 00:29:56.617
Irina and I were up all night.

00:29:56.694 --> 00:29:58.457
Oh, really?

00:29:58.530 --> 00:29:59.622
Making repairs.

00:29:59.697 --> 00:30:00.629
Uh-huh.

00:30:00.698 --> 00:30:02.689
To be honest, I can't remember

00:30:02.767 --> 00:30:04.928
the last time
I had so much fun.

00:30:05.036 --> 00:30:06.469
She's funny, smart,

00:30:06.538 --> 00:30:09.166
we get along without trying.

00:30:09.240 --> 00:30:10.571
I'm going to ask her
if she wants

00:30:10.642 --> 00:30:12.542
to spend some time
on Voyager after the race.

00:30:12.610 --> 00:30:14.703
What about Joxom?

00:30:14.779 --> 00:30:17.179
Turns out
they're just teammates.

00:30:17.248 --> 00:30:19.580
I know what you're going to say.

00:30:19.651 --> 00:30:20.709
No, no.

00:30:20.785 --> 00:30:23.049
Actually, I was just
going to congratulate you.

00:30:23.121 --> 00:30:24.952
I mean, she's not a Borg,
she's not a hologram

00:30:25.056 --> 00:30:27.524
and she's not dead.

00:30:27.592 --> 00:30:29.287
Looks like you might have
finally found yourself

00:30:29.360 --> 00:30:30.292
the perfect woman.

00:30:30.361 --> 00:30:32.226
All teams report to your ships.

00:30:32.297 --> 00:30:34.128
The race will resume
in 30 minutes.

00:30:34.199 --> 00:30:37.191
See you on the course.

00:30:49.547 --> 00:30:50.878
Attention all hands.

00:30:50.949 --> 00:30:53.247
Stand by
for another race update.

00:30:53.318 --> 00:30:55.115
After fighting off
a formidable challenge

00:30:55.186 --> 00:30:57.211
from the Terrellian team,

00:30:57.288 --> 00:30:59.415
the Delta Flyer has managed
to hold onto its lead

00:30:59.490 --> 00:31:01.185
going into the third
and final segment.

00:31:07.765 --> 00:31:10.097
Approaching the pulsars.

00:31:10.168 --> 00:31:12.602
"Straight through the gate."

00:31:12.670 --> 00:31:14.604
"Then remodulate."

00:31:14.672 --> 00:31:17.766
Harry sure had that glow,
didn't he?

00:31:17.842 --> 00:31:18.900
What glow?

00:31:18.977 --> 00:31:20.239
You know,

00:31:20.311 --> 00:31:22.506
that look you get
when you first meet someone.

00:31:22.580 --> 00:31:25.276
Yeah. His cheeks were
a little redder than usual.

00:31:25.350 --> 00:31:28.342
We're through the pulsars.

00:31:28.419 --> 00:31:30.785
Harry and Irina
are right behind us.

00:31:30.855 --> 00:31:32.948
You can ease up
off the thrusters now.

00:31:33.024 --> 00:31:36.289
I want to conserve some fuel
for the final leg.

00:31:36.361 --> 00:31:38.090
If circumstances were right,

00:31:38.162 --> 00:31:40.653
they might even have
a future together.

00:31:40.732 --> 00:31:41.858
What?

00:31:41.933 --> 00:31:44.128
Harry and Irina.

00:31:44.202 --> 00:31:45.226
Oh, they just met.

00:31:45.303 --> 00:31:47.965
It's a little early
to be planning a wedding.

00:31:48.072 --> 00:31:51.200
No, I just meant that some
people just fit together

00:31:51.276 --> 00:31:52.971
without having to work at it.

00:31:53.077 --> 00:31:55.978
And other people,
no matter how much they try...

00:31:56.114 --> 00:31:58.708
Are we talking about them or us?

00:31:58.783 --> 00:31:59.943
What?

00:32:02.020 --> 00:32:03.351
No, I didn't mean...

00:32:03.421 --> 00:32:06.151
If something's bothering you,
let's talk about it.

00:32:08.159 --> 00:32:10.127
We should concentrate
on the race.

00:32:16.067 --> 00:32:17.500
Well, maybe Harry and Irina

00:32:17.568 --> 00:32:19.399
aren't such a great team
after all.

00:32:19.470 --> 00:32:21.938
They're falling behind.

00:32:22.040 --> 00:32:24.338
I'm reading malfunctions
in the EPS relays,

00:32:24.409 --> 00:32:26.673
but we double-checked
all of them last night.

00:32:26.744 --> 00:32:28.075
We must have missed something.

00:32:28.146 --> 00:32:30.239
At this rate, we're going
to be out of the race

00:32:30.315 --> 00:32:31.612
in a couple of minutes.

00:32:31.683 --> 00:32:35.517
I think I can reroute power
through the impulse manifold.

00:32:35.586 --> 00:32:36.518
No.

00:32:36.587 --> 00:32:38.851
Why not?

00:32:38.923 --> 00:32:41.118
It could damage
the reactor coils.

00:32:41.192 --> 00:32:42.955
What do the reactor coils
have to do

00:32:43.094 --> 00:32:44.527
with the impulse manifolds?

00:32:44.595 --> 00:32:46.961
These systems are different
than what you're used to.

00:32:47.065 --> 00:32:50.330
You do want to win, don't you?

00:32:51.402 --> 00:32:53.393
Of course I do.

00:32:53.471 --> 00:32:57.464
It just seems like every time
I make a suggestion,

00:32:57.542 --> 00:32:59.976
you find a reason to reject it.

00:33:00.111 --> 00:33:03.080
I'm more familiar
with my ship than you are.

00:33:04.215 --> 00:33:05.204
Now what?

00:33:05.283 --> 00:33:07.717
I think it's the injector ports.

00:33:07.785 --> 00:33:11.152
No, it's an overload
in my console.

00:33:15.426 --> 00:33:18.657
That's the second time
your copilot's console exploded.

00:33:18.730 --> 00:33:20.357
Quite a coincidence.

00:33:21.666 --> 00:33:23.725
I'm sorry, Harry.

00:33:23.801 --> 00:33:25.530
I really am.

00:33:31.542 --> 00:33:33.476
You sabotaged your own ship...

00:33:33.544 --> 00:33:35.637
twice.

00:33:35.713 --> 00:33:39.740
Why are you trying so hard
to get out of this race?

00:33:51.396 --> 00:33:53.125
What the hell is going on?

00:33:54.365 --> 00:33:55.798
Sit down and hold still!

00:34:02.306 --> 00:34:03.637
All right.

00:34:03.708 --> 00:34:05.801
If you won't talk to me,

00:34:05.877 --> 00:34:08.641
maybe you'll talk
to Antarian Security.

00:34:11.682 --> 00:34:13.741
You disabled the com system.

00:34:15.253 --> 00:34:16.481
We'll just wait.

00:34:16.554 --> 00:34:19.318
Someone will come along
eventually.

00:34:24.862 --> 00:34:26.762
We're past the last marker.

00:34:26.831 --> 00:34:28.799
Time to deploy the thrusters?

00:34:28.866 --> 00:34:30.197
Whatever you say.

00:34:30.268 --> 00:34:32.964
What happened
to "I'm the pilot"?

00:34:34.038 --> 00:34:36.871
That really bothered you,
didn't it?

00:34:36.941 --> 00:34:37.930
It's why you think

00:34:38.042 --> 00:34:40.476
we don't fit together
as well as Harry and Irina?

00:34:40.545 --> 00:34:41.807
Could we talk about this later?

00:34:41.879 --> 00:34:43.141
Assan is gaining on us.

00:34:43.214 --> 00:34:45.512
Well, then, I guess you'd better
deploy the thrusters.

00:34:45.583 --> 00:34:47.710
Thrusters deployed.

00:34:49.654 --> 00:34:52.122
This isn't about the race
anymore, is it?

00:34:52.190 --> 00:34:53.657
You tell me.

00:35:00.731 --> 00:35:02.426
If we're going to just sit here,

00:35:02.500 --> 00:35:04.400
we might as well see
who's winning.

00:35:04.469 --> 00:35:07.404
You're not exactly in a position
to be making requests.

00:35:07.472 --> 00:35:11.568
Admit it, Harry...
you're curious, too.

00:35:18.382 --> 00:35:20.646
The Delta Flyer is still
in the lead.

00:35:20.718 --> 00:35:24.210
Good for them.

00:35:26.757 --> 00:35:29.453
I thought that if we could
do this one thing together,

00:35:29.527 --> 00:35:31.051
something that you cared about,

00:35:31.129 --> 00:35:32.926
that it might help
our relationship.

00:35:32.997 --> 00:35:34.658
I didn't know it needed help.

00:35:34.732 --> 00:35:37.166
Well, that's part
of the problem.

00:35:37.235 --> 00:35:39.533
What's the rest?

00:35:39.604 --> 00:35:40.901
You know the rest.

00:35:42.974 --> 00:35:45.875
So we scrape shields
occasionally.

00:35:45.943 --> 00:35:47.877
It keeps things interesting.

00:35:47.945 --> 00:35:50.175
Maybe interesting
isn't enough for me.

00:35:54.185 --> 00:35:55.675
What are you doing?

00:35:55.753 --> 00:35:57.380
They're stopping.

00:35:57.455 --> 00:35:59.286
They're dead in the water.

00:35:59.357 --> 00:36:00.255
Ah-ah.

00:36:03.661 --> 00:36:05.595
How far from the finish line?

00:36:05.663 --> 00:36:07.961
Less than a million kilometers.

00:36:11.602 --> 00:36:13.331
That was Assan!

00:36:13.404 --> 00:36:15.235
Why are we just sitting here?

00:36:15.306 --> 00:36:16.705
If we've got a problem,

00:36:16.774 --> 00:36:19.902
we're going to resolve it
right here, right now.

00:36:20.011 --> 00:36:21.911
You've done everything possible
to take yourself

00:36:22.013 --> 00:36:24.447
out of the race,
and now you seem worried

00:36:24.515 --> 00:36:27.006
that the Delta Flyer
won't reach the finish line.

00:36:30.588 --> 00:36:31.919
I'm counting more than a dozen

00:36:32.056 --> 00:36:35.423
ships there...
spectators, officials...

00:36:35.493 --> 00:36:38.553
All congregated
in the name of peace.

00:36:38.629 --> 00:36:40.187
Touching, isn't it?

00:36:40.264 --> 00:36:42.926
You've planned
some sort of attack.

00:36:43.034 --> 00:36:46.470
There are hundreds of
innocent people there.

00:36:46.537 --> 00:36:48.129
How can you do that?

00:36:49.373 --> 00:36:53.139
Not everyone is as comfortable
mixing with other species

00:36:53.211 --> 00:36:54.371
as you are, Harry.

00:36:54.445 --> 00:36:58.176
Some of us believe it was better
when we were separate.

00:36:58.249 --> 00:36:59.807
Hey, I never asked you
to give up this race,

00:36:59.884 --> 00:37:01.476
or anything else
that you care about.

00:37:01.552 --> 00:37:03.315
I never asked you
to stop being yourself.

00:37:03.387 --> 00:37:04.877
The only self that I want to be

00:37:04.989 --> 00:37:06.854
is the guy
that you're in love with.

00:37:06.924 --> 00:37:11.691
Wow... I didn't know
you felt that way.

00:37:11.762 --> 00:37:13.525
How can you say that?

00:37:15.800 --> 00:37:18.735
Well, you always seem
to have other priorities.

00:37:18.803 --> 00:37:22.136
I'm showing you my priorities
right now.

00:37:22.206 --> 00:37:24.538
The Delta Flyer wouldn't even be
in this race

00:37:24.609 --> 00:37:26.270
if you hadn't told us about it.

00:37:26.344 --> 00:37:30.371
You gave us the fuel converter
so we could qualify.

00:37:30.448 --> 00:37:32.382
The fuel converter.

00:37:32.450 --> 00:37:34.008
That's why you're so concerned

00:37:34.085 --> 00:37:37.248
about Tom and B'Elanna's
crossing the finish line.

00:37:37.321 --> 00:37:39.255
What'd you do to it?

00:37:39.323 --> 00:37:41.018
Rig it to explode?

00:37:48.766 --> 00:37:51.633
How come you never talked
to me about this before?

00:37:51.702 --> 00:37:56.401
Well, you've got that tough
Klingon exterior, and...

00:37:56.474 --> 00:37:59.409
I didn't think you liked
the mushy stuff.

00:37:59.477 --> 00:38:02.412
Do I look that tough right now?

00:38:02.480 --> 00:38:07.417
Well, does that mean you're in
the mood for some mushy stuff?

00:38:07.485 --> 00:38:09.578
Maybe.

00:38:09.654 --> 00:38:12.748
Exactly what kind of mush
are we talking about?

00:38:12.823 --> 00:38:15.758
You tell me.

00:38:15.826 --> 00:38:19.125
Well, there's, um...

00:38:23.234 --> 00:38:25.327
kissy stuff.

00:38:25.403 --> 00:38:29.100
That was nice.

00:38:29.173 --> 00:38:31.767
And there's the...

00:38:31.842 --> 00:38:35.608
"you're the most important
person in the world to me."

00:38:35.680 --> 00:38:37.910
I like that one, too.

00:38:38.015 --> 00:38:42.918
And there's
the "happily ever after."

00:38:43.020 --> 00:38:45.079
How does that one work?

00:38:46.691 --> 00:38:51.253
Well, traditionally,
it requires a proposal...

00:38:59.670 --> 00:39:03.071
We're being scanned by some kind
of modulating pulse.

00:39:03.140 --> 00:39:04.573
It's from Irina's ship.

00:39:04.642 --> 00:39:07.008
They must be wondering
why we stopped.

00:39:07.078 --> 00:39:09.012
There's something odd
about the amplitude.

00:39:09.080 --> 00:39:10.843
Wait a minute.
Di-di-da...

00:39:10.915 --> 00:39:14.248
That's Morse code.

00:39:14.318 --> 00:39:17.412
Harry and I use it in the
Captain Proton holoprogram.

00:39:17.488 --> 00:39:18.887
What's he saying?

00:39:19.023 --> 00:39:24.017
"Fuel... converter...

00:39:24.095 --> 00:39:25.824
"rigged.

00:39:25.896 --> 00:39:26.988
Eject."

00:39:27.064 --> 00:39:28.793
What does he mean by "rigged"?

00:39:28.866 --> 00:39:31.835
That converter's leaking
veridium isotopes.

00:39:31.902 --> 00:39:34.496
Why didn't the computer warn us?

00:39:34.572 --> 00:39:37.302
The on-line sensors
have been tampered with.

00:39:37.375 --> 00:39:39.104
Can you contain the leak?

00:39:39.176 --> 00:39:40.768
Too late. The veridium
is already reacting

00:39:40.845 --> 00:39:41.777
with the warp plasma.

00:39:41.846 --> 00:39:43.643
That'll cause
a warp core breach.

00:39:43.714 --> 00:39:44.612
In less than a minute.

00:39:44.682 --> 00:39:45.614
Then do what Harry said.

00:39:45.683 --> 00:39:46.513
Eject the converter.

00:39:46.584 --> 00:39:47.516
It's too late.

00:39:47.585 --> 00:39:48.813
I have to eject the core.

00:39:48.886 --> 00:39:50.012
Here?

00:39:50.087 --> 00:39:52.317
We'll never survive the blast.

00:39:52.390 --> 00:39:56.349
Neither will anyone else
within a million kilometers.

00:39:57.928 --> 00:39:59.361
They're moving again.

00:40:02.333 --> 00:40:05.825
Away... from the finish line.

00:40:12.143 --> 00:40:14.703
Warp core breach in 30 seconds.

00:40:14.779 --> 00:40:16.940
Where are we going?

00:40:17.014 --> 00:40:18.914
A J-class nebula
filled with ionized gas.

00:40:18.983 --> 00:40:20.143
Should contain the explosion.

00:40:20.217 --> 00:40:22.947
I can't get the ejection
subroutines on line.

00:40:23.087 --> 00:40:25.078
Warp core breach in 20 seconds.

00:40:25.156 --> 00:40:27.420
So what's your answer?

00:40:27.491 --> 00:40:28.583
My answer?

00:40:28.659 --> 00:40:31.287
Will you marry me?

00:40:31.362 --> 00:40:33.455
Warp core breach in 15 seconds.

00:40:33.531 --> 00:40:34.964
You're proposing now?

00:40:35.032 --> 00:40:36.294
It's as good a time as any.

00:40:36.367 --> 00:40:38.835
Subroutines back on line.

00:40:38.903 --> 00:40:41.371
Warp core breach in ten seconds,
nine, eight...

00:40:44.975 --> 00:40:45.907
Clear!

00:40:45.976 --> 00:40:46.840
...four...
- Go!

00:40:46.911 --> 00:40:47.935
...three...

00:41:02.259 --> 00:41:03.453
Damn.

00:41:07.898 --> 00:41:11.334
I'm sorry your team
didn't win, Captain.

00:41:11.402 --> 00:41:13.336
Janeway to the Bridge.
Report.

00:41:13.404 --> 00:41:16.862
That was a shock wave
from an antimatter explosion

00:41:16.941 --> 00:41:19.842
approximately 1.2 million
kilometers from here.

00:41:19.910 --> 00:41:21.207
Excuse me.

00:41:28.853 --> 00:41:30.616
B'Elanna...

00:41:33.791 --> 00:41:35.224
I guess we lost.

00:41:35.292 --> 00:41:37.226
That depends.

00:41:37.294 --> 00:41:39.091
On what?

00:41:39.163 --> 00:41:41.757
On how you answer my question.

00:41:41.832 --> 00:41:43.732
I thought you only asked it

00:41:43.801 --> 00:41:46.201
because we were
about to explode.

00:41:46.270 --> 00:41:48.534
Well, we're still alive...

00:41:48.606 --> 00:41:50.506
and I'm still asking.

00:41:53.711 --> 00:41:55.804
How come you never
asked me before?

00:41:55.880 --> 00:41:57.438
How come you're still
avoiding the question?

00:41:57.515 --> 00:41:58.447
I'm thinking.

00:41:58.516 --> 00:41:59.710
Think faster.

00:41:59.783 --> 00:42:01.478
Why? You're gonna
withdraw the question?

00:42:01.552 --> 00:42:03.884
No, but I might start to beg.

00:42:03.954 --> 00:42:05.854
Could get embarrassing.

00:42:08.859 --> 00:42:11.692
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:42:11.762 --> 00:42:13.787
The Antarians have invited us

00:42:13.864 --> 00:42:16.230
to participate
in the post-race festivities,

00:42:16.300 --> 00:42:19.428
which has allowed me to give
two of my senior officers

00:42:19.503 --> 00:42:22.631
time off for a well-deserved
romantic getaway.

00:42:22.706 --> 00:42:25.334
The Delta Flyer still needs
a new warp core,

00:42:25.409 --> 00:42:28.742
but I don't think they're
in a hurry to get anywhere.

00:42:28.812 --> 00:42:32.111
To... the winners.

00:42:37.154 --> 00:42:40.248
"B'Elanna Paris"...
that has a nice ring to it.

00:42:40.324 --> 00:42:42.292
Thanks, but I
already have a ring.

00:42:44.328 --> 00:42:47.786
Anyway, I kind of like
the sound of "Tom Torres."

00:42:47.865 --> 00:42:49.730
I hope you're kidding.

00:42:49.800 --> 00:42:53.292
Hey... it is the 24th century.
